A place keeps the core it last waited on as it is bound to another core's units, and waits on that core's queues,
where its thread takes the time of a core it holds none of; a queued place waits on the core its units are of.

Caught-by: fuzz-smp2
Report: a place waits on another core than its units are of
Witness: fuzz-smp2 cores-actor-waits-release

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -389,7 +389,8 @@ static void place_settle(struct place *p)
         account_refill(p);
     }
     struct core *was = &cores[p->core];
-    struct core *core = &cores[place_core(p)];
+    struct core *core = &cores[p->core];
+    (void)place_core;
     const struct place *l = has_time(p->balance) ? NULL : place_lender(p);
     uint8_t queue = place_queue(p, p->balance, l);
     bool joined = queue != QUEUE_NONE && (queue != p->queue || core != was);
